{"id": 9251, "doi": "10.4038/slja.v32i1.9251", "title": "Spinal Myoclonus a Rare Complication Following Administration of Spinal Anaeasthesia &ndash; A Case Report", "abstract": "<p>Spinal myoclonus is a rare complication following spinal anesthesia. Transient myoclonic jerks are referred as spinal myoclonus and it is diagnosed by exclusion. This case report describes a successful management of spinal myoclonus after spinal anesthesia.<br />A 48 year old, woman who had undergone incision and drainage under spinal anesthesia, developed truncal myoclonus 45 minutes following induction of anesthesia. It was effectively alleviated through administration of IV midazolam.</p>", "keywords": [], "authors": [{"first_name": "K. A. M. S. P.", "last_name": "Kandearachchi", "institution": "Base Hospital, Kantale", "country": "LK", "email": "milankandearachchi@gmail.com", "orcid": ""}, {"first_name": "A. G. H.", "last_name": "Menike", "institution": "Base Hospital, Kantale", "country": "LK", "email": "", "orcid": ""}, {"first_name": "K. G.", "last_name": "Madawala", "institution": "Base Hospital, Kantale", "country": "LK", "email": "", "orcid": ""}, {"first_name": "H. H.", "last_name": "Sarathchandra", "institution": "Base Hospital, Kantale", "country": "LK", "email": "", "orcid": ""}, {"first_name": "N. L. S. H.", "last_name": "Jayawardana", "institution": "Base Hospital, Kantale", "country": "LK", "email": "", "orcid": ""}, {"first_name": "H. R. R.", "last_name": "Kulasiri", "institution": "Base Hospital, Kantale", "country": "LK", "email": "", "orcid": ""}, {"first_name": "D. I. J.", "last_name": "Samarasekara", "institution": "Base Hospital, Kantale", "country": "LK", "email": "", "orcid": ""}], "section": "Case Reports", "pages": "74-78", "date_published": "2024-01-30T00:00:00+00:00", "date_submitted": "2023-07-22T19:17:22+00:00", "license_name": "CC Attribution 4.0", "license_link": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0", "files": [{"label": "PDF", "language": "en", 